From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:40:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] rutabaga_gfx(macos): wmtr context type for remoted DXMT
 winemetal calls

Add an opt-in virtio-gpu context type (capset 30, "wmtr") whose guest
process forwards DXMT's winemetal unix calls through a shared-memory
ring to a host executor that runs them against Metal. The executor is a
separate library (libwmtr_host.dylib, STEAMAC_WMTR_LIB or the default
name) loaded with dlopen and used only if its wmtr_host_abi_version() is
the one this patch implements (1: create, kick, progress, destroy and
wmtr_layout, and two callbacks, blob_ptr and wake); this patch only
carries the transport:

- blobs (blob_id = ring/buffer number below 1024, checked before
  narrowing to u32; live ids unique; size at most max_blob, 4 GiB) are
  POSIX shared memory, mapped into the guest by the existing SHM blob
  path and into the VMM for the executor. CTX_DETACH_RESOURCE reaches
  the context's detach before RESOURCE_UNREF drops the VMM's mapping
  and descriptor (unref itself only reaches the component). Detach
  forgets an arena blob and overlays the context's mapping with fresh
  MAP_FIXED | MAP_ANON | MAP_PRIVATE memory: the shm pages leave the
  footprint once the VMM unmaps and unrefs it, but the address range
  remains reserved until context teardown for stale executor pointers.
  The released number can be created again; the client must release
  only idle arenas with no live ranges or host buffers. Blob 0 is the
  ring and is never released before executor teardown;
- EXECBUFFER carries 24-byte commands: RING (blob 0 is initialised:
  start the executor; refused when blob 0, sized by the guest, is
  smaller than the ring layout the library reports through wmtr_layout,
  as the executor uses fixed offsets up to it), KICK (wake it), WAIT
  (the fence of this EXECBUFFER completes when the executor's reply
  slot reaches the sequence number; every WAIT of an EXECBUFFER holds
  its fence, and WAITs of an EXECBUFFER without a fence, or of a
  refused one, hold none; progress is checked and the waiter queued
  under one lock, so a reply cannot slip between them, and RING
  re-checks queued fences once the executor handle is stored, so a
  reply during wmtr_host_create is not lost); a command buffer that is
  not a whole number of commands is refused; each (context, ring) is an in-order
  timeline, and reply slots share rings (slot s on ring 1 + s % 62,
  events and slots >= 64 on ring 63, as the guest maps them), so the
  fences of a ring complete strictly in FIFO order: one whose WAIT
  already holds, or that has no WAIT, waits behind an earlier pending
  one; pending fences complete when the context is destroyed;
- teardown takes the executor handle out under its lock before
  wmtr_host_destroy, so a wake during destroy never reaches the executor
  being freed; the library runs no callback after wmtr_host_destroy
  returns, and the context frees its state and mappings only then;
  the library must not call wake while holding a lock that
  wmtr_host_progress takes, and checks the guest's slot and ring
  contents itself;
- the capset id is below 32 because VIRTGPU_PARAM_SUPPORTED_CAPSET_IDs
  reports a 32-bit mask; no stock rutabaga capset uses 30.

The component exists only with STEAMAC_WMTR=1 and a loadable library
that exports the host API (one cached load shared by the device's config
space and the rutabaga builder). Then num_capsets counts it: the stock 5
covers virgl, virgl2, venus, drm and cross-domain, and the guest never
asks for an index at or above that count. Without it nothing changes: no
library is loaded and the guest sees the same five capsets.

Unit tests (15, cargo test --lib wmtr in rutabaga_gfx, against a stand-in
executor: no Metal, no library): off unless enabled; a WAIT fence stays
pending until the reply and completes on it; satisfied WAITs and fences
without a WAIT complete at once on an otherwise idle ring; pending
fences complete on context drop and the executor is destroyed; malformed
blobs and commands are rejected; on a shared ring (slots 0 and 62,
events and slot 70) later fences wait for an earlier pending one and
complete with it, in order; live duplicate blob ids, ids at or above 1024 (1 <<
32, u64::MAX) and blobs over max_blob are rejected and leave the
existing blob in place; RING on a blob 0 smaller than the ring layout
is refused before the executor starts; a library without
wmtr_host_abi_version, with another version, with part of the API or
without wmtr_layout is refused; a wake delivered
while the executor is destroyed does not call into it; two WAITs of one
EXECBUFFER (slots 0 and 62) both hold its fence; WAITs of an EXECBUFFER
without a fence or of a refused one hold no later fence; a reply from
inside wmtr_host_create completes the fence waiting for it when RING
returns; a partial command is refused; a detached 64 MiB arena leaves
at least 90% of its size from the process footprint after unref, stops
resolving and leaves fresh writable anonymous memory at its old address;
its number can be created again (but not duplicated while live), and
blob 0 survives detach and unref while the executor keeps running.
Before the detach change, the three arena release tests fail: footprint
65 -> 65 MiB, released blob still resolves, and recreated id is refused.
virtio::gpu (12 tests): num_capsets stays 5 without STEAMAC_WMTR.
